From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:21:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-taimen: Easel powers off in
 suspend

Easel removes its own power during the first system sleep; the link
never comes back and the kernel cannot restore it. Mark the root port
with endpoint-powered-off-in-suspend so qcom-pcie keeps the controller
powered and untouched across sleep instead of running the link-down
host_deinit()/host_init() pair against the dead partner, which wedges
the SoC interconnect on the second s2idle cycle (measured: 5/5 hangs
attributed to dpm_resume_noirq at 1c00000.pcie / 0000:00:00.0; with
the controller left untouched, 85/85 clean cycles).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
index c1a0594a438c..5839108cbfed 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
@@ -642,6 +642,19 @@ &pcie0 {
 	 * suppresses bind attrs, so there is no way to retry afterwards.
 	 */
 	vddpe-3v3-supply = <&easel_vddpe>;
+
+	pcie@0 {
+		/*
+		 * Easel powers itself off the bus during the first system
+		 * sleep and only its own PMIC/firmware can bring it back.
+		 * Tell the controller driver, so it leaves the port alone
+		 * across suspend instead of powering the host off on the
+		 * link-down suspend and reinitializing it on resume against
+		 * the absent partner -- which wedges the SoC interconnect,
+		 * deterministically, on the second s2idle cycle.
+		 */
+		endpoint-powered-off-in-suspend;
+	};
 };
 
 &blsp2_i2c3 {
